-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Green Beret
  Publisher   Imagine, 1986
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Green Beret (1986)(Imagine)[a2][a2].z80
  MD5         c1a76349d08289810323bae0e62a9102

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Pace        original (+0.00% measured in JNext 1.1.104 headless, the v2.09
              card; probe 0xA38C (the main loop's scenery blit, once a game
              update); input keyed to updates; lockstep on lives and stage; 10
              trials per scene of up to 300 updates (the mean; single trials
              0.00 to +0.21 percent, never faster: the game waits for the
              interrupt each update))

  Changes     1.0: figures as Next sprites (white body, black dark pixels, a 1
              pixel white edge around each outline); Sinclair's 48K ROM as the
              whole alt ROM; the game's speed restored after every hook

  Note        Keys: 1 on the game's menu for the keyboard, then your six keys
              (up, down, left, right, stab, shoot), Y, then stab to start. The
              player, soldiers, dogs and explosions are Next sprites in white
              and black over their own pixels; scenery, panel and text keep
              the original's colours. Each figure keeps a 1 pixel white edge
              so it stays clear of dark scenery. Pace is the original's (the
              game waits for each frame). Tested in JNext on NextZXOS v2.09
              and v2.10. Known issues: the beeper makes 5 to 7 percent fewer
              writes than the original, so some sound effects may sound
              slightly different; in the sky the figures' white bodies are
              solid, because the original draws them there without a mask; the
              weapon shot is drawn behind the figures. Missing: no Enhanced
              colour set yet (figures are white and black only); no loading or
              title screen on the menu; the cheats are the archive's POKEs and
              were not re-checked in this build; hardware untested.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives
   2  Extra firepower
   3  No mines
   4  Infinite ammo
   5  Immunity (except mortars)
   6  Mortars don't shoot

  Cheats are the archive's POKEs for this release; dropped: Lives and the
  weapon choice (they ask for a value).

