-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      Played by the owner in JNext 2026-11-06: approved

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 4 recordings, 84,814 frames: 22,521 draw passes,
              91,412 figure plots, 2,716 object plots, 9,871 mines, 4,119
              bullets, 40 screen wipes: at every hook original and patched
              code compared from the same state (every register but R, all
              memory), then the picture: the patched screen plus the sprites
              against the original's pixels, 35.2M pixels; the trimmed edge
              pixels (310,485 in 54,983 plots) allowed only where a plot of a
              trimmed figure put them; 106 figure images against the edge
              rule, 18 negative controls detected (the edge rule left out and
              the exit forced to 3.5 MHz among them). R is not kept by the
              hooks: the game reads R only for its bit 7 (the sign after LD
              A,R), and the four recordings replayed with R's low 7 bits
              randomised at every hook site and game update (283,838 times)
              give the same RAM at every update

  Emulator    JNext 1.1.104 headless. On copies of the v2.09 and the 26.11
              (NextZXOS v2.10) emulator cards, through the Browser: the .nxc
              and the loader's menu, then ENTER: the loader wrote the bare
              build (d982d5ae) on both, and the game reached play, the same
              pictures at the same frames on both cards; the menu .nex the
              same. The whole alt ROM image copies no NextZXOS ROM3 byte, so
              the v2.10 ROM3 change does not reach it. Flicker check over 300
              frames of play: 0 frames out of step, 0 vanished figures, 0 one-
              frame attribute changes or transients; 15-minute soak against
              the original: no freeze, loop or crash (game overs and restarts
              in both); pace as below

  Coverage    Random-key recordings only, no human play: stages 1-4 reached
              (lives, immunity and weapon cheats in some recordings'
              snapshots), deaths, game over and restart, weapons and pickups;
              not reached: the end of stage 3 by play (by cheat only), stage
              4's boss paths, the end of the game

  Hardware    none

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
